time=2025-12-22T18:07:25.321+01:00 level=TRACE source=sentencepiece.go:188 msg=encoded string="<start_of_turn>user\n### System:\nYou are issue-fixer. ISSUE-FIXER:Autonomous agent to diagnose, propose, and apply fixes on GitHub repositories. (invoked by user 5)\nYour personal goal is: In the repository git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git, resolve the GitHub issue number 1 locally and propose PRs. Context: run by user_id=5. Local environment 'dummy_agent', owner='DjoserKhemSimeu', repo='dummy_agent'.$$$RUN_ID: USER_ID=5 NB_USER=10 MODEL=gemma3:4b ITER=0 HOST=http://127.0.0.1:53100$$$\nYou ONLY have access to the following tools, and should NEVER make up tools that are not listed here:\n\nTool Name: git_clone\nTool Arguments: {'repo_url': {'description': 'SSH of the GitHub repository to clone', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Clone a GitHub repository locally (uses the `git` CLI) and change into the cloned directory.\nTool Name: read_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Reads a file in the cloned repository and returns its content.\nTool Name: write_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}, 'content': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Writes content to a file in the cloned repository (creates directories if needed).\nTool Name: run_tests\nTool Arguments: {'pytest_args': {'description': None, 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Runs the test suite via `pytest` if present in the repository.\nTool Name: git_commit\nTool Arguments: {'message': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Stage and commit changes in the local repository.\nTool Name: git_push\nTool Arguments: {'force': {'description': None, 'type': 'bool'}}\nTool Description: Pushes the local branch to the 'origin' remote.\nTool Name: fetch_issue\nTool Arguments: {'owner': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}, 'repo': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}, 'issue_number': {'description': None, 'type': 'int'}}\nTool Description: Fetches issues from the GitHub API.\n\nIMPORTANT: Use the following format in your response:\n\n```\nThought: you should always think about what to do\nAction: the action to take, only one name of [git_clone, read_file, write_file, run_tests, git_commit, git_push, fetch_issue], just the name, exactly as it's written.\nAction Input: the input to the action, just a simple JSON object, enclosed in curly braces, using \" to wrap keys and values.\nObservation: the result of the action\n```\n\nOnce all necessary information is gathered, return the following format:\n\n```\nThought: I now know the final answer\nFinal Answer: the final answer to the original input question\n```\n\n### User:\n\nCurrent Task: TASK-PLANNER:Fix the provided issue: clone the repo, diagnose, propose a patch, and create a PR if tests pass. The update pipeline should be the following:\n1. Clone the GitHub repository locally and jump into it.\n2. Create a new branch for the changes.\n3. Analyze the issue and the code to identify the root of the issue.\n4. Make the necessary changes to the source code.\n5. Run the test suite to validate the changes.\n6. If tests pass, commit the changes and push the branch to the remote repository.\n$$$RUN_ID: USER_ID=5 NB_USER=10 MODEL=gemma3:4b ITER=0 HOST=http://127.0.0.1:53100$$$\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: Report of the actions taken, including the URL of the created branch pushed.\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nBegin! This is VERY important to you, use the tools available and give your best Final Answer, your job depends on it!\n\nThought:\n\n### Assistant:\nOkay, let's start by cloning the repository. I need the repository URL to do that. Since I don't have that information yet, I'll first use the `fetch_issue` tool to get the repository URL.\nAction: fetch_issue\nAction Input: {'owner': 'DjoserKhemSimeu', 'repo': 'dummy_agent', 'issue_number': 1}\nObservation: Bonjour,\n\nLorsque j'exécute `app.py`, une erreur apparaît :\n\n    NameError: name 'c' is not defined\n\nLa fonction `addition(a, b)` utilise `c` alors que cette variable n'existe pas.  \nLa ligne suivante pose problème :\n\n    return a + c\n\nSolution attendue : remplacer `c` par `b`.\n\nMerci !Thought: I need to clone the repository and then fix the `NameError`. I will start by cloning the repository using the `git_clone` tool.\nAction: git_clone\nAction Input: {'repo_url': 'git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git'}\nObservation: Clone error: Command '['git', 'clone', 'git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git']' returned non-zero exit status 128.\n\n<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\nThought: The clone failed. I need to try again, but this time I will explicitly specify the clone directory.\nAction: git_clone\nAction Input: {'repo_url': 'git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git', 'path': 'dummy_agent'}" ids="[105 2364 107 10354 1804 236787 107 3048 659 4186 236772 9462 497 236761 170435 236772 51022 1089 236787 209380 8726 531 58355 236764 20017 236764 532 5510 49048 580 34115 82341 236761 568 18034 15320 684 2430 236743 236810 236768 107 11069 3577 5671 563 236787 799 506 20387 23032 236940 5846 236761 854 236787 236796 21434 497 236855 12427 236773 764 236756 236786 49152 236779 20154 236761 13705 236764 14245 506 34115 4186 1548 236743 236770 16445 532 20017 9206 236751 236761 17605 236787 1845 684 2430 236779 547 236784 236810 236761 12263 3453 756 49152 236779 20154 963 8123 2507 236796 21434 497 236855 12427 236773 764 236756 963 34691 2507 49152 236779 20154 6748 9873 236795 45562 236779 1735 236787 33181 236779 1735 236784 236810 55740 236779 20791 236784 236770 236771 61507 236784 236759 12367 236800 236787 236812 236763 202418 236784 236771 134784 236784 2855 1411 236770 236778 236832 236761 236771 236761 236771 236761 236770 236787 236810 236800 236770 236771 236771 9873 236795 107 3048 4